I walk over to the counter.
I have a thick, red sweater in my hands.
I also have a long, blue scarf and warm, black gloves.
The shop assistant waits behind the counter.
She smiles at me.
I put all the clothes on the counter.
The shop assistant takes the red sweater.
She scans it quickly.
Then she takes the blue scarf.
Finally, she scans the black gloves.
"Those are some warm things," the shop assistant says.
"Yes, it is very cold outside," I answer.
She looks at her screen.
"That will be six hundred and fifty kroner," she says.
"I am paying with a card," I say.
I take out my payment card.
I hold the card over the terminal.
The machine beeps loudly.
The payment is approved.
"Do you want a bag for the clothes?" she asks.
